1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,944
The operator confirms the
frame in their own words.

2
00:00:03,014 --> 00:00:08,369
Review the workflow boundary, measurement
definition, fixed constraints, proposed experiment,

3
00:00:08,439 --> 00:00:09,953
and decision authority.

4
00:00:10,023 --> 00:00:12,327
Disagreement is useful evidence.

5
00:00:12,397 --> 00:00:17,347
Record exclusions so nobody mistakes a
local test for a production commitment.

6
00:00:17,417 --> 00:00:20,297
Keep the initial frame
version when you revise it.

7
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:26,105
If conditions change before acting, document
the change and obtain the relevant agreement

8
00:00:26,175 --> 00:00:28,245
within the simulated engagement.

9
00:00:28,315 --> 00:00:31,515
Maya approves assisted
routing for access tickets.

10
00:00:31,585 --> 00:00:33,867
Priya approves only synthetic data.

11
00:00:33,937 --> 00:00:36,647
The sponsor still expects automatic replies.

12
00:00:36,717 --> 00:00:42,647
Your decision record must expose this difference
before anyone calls the experiment a customer

13
00:00:42,717 --> 00:00:43,784
deployment.

14
00:00:43,854 --> 00:00:48,633
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

15
00:00:48,703 --> 00:00:53,759
Write a scope note naming included work,
excluded work, owners, and the next gate.

16
00:00:53,829 --> 00:00:58,565
Included: synthetic access-ticket routing,
reviewer approval, and event logging.

17
00:00:58,635 --> 00:01:04,587
Excluded: customer replies, production credentials,
staffing promises, and model procurement.

18
00:01:04,657 --> 00:01:06,790
Maya reviews workflow usefulness.

19
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:10,039
Priya retains authority over future data access.

20
00:01:10,109 --> 00:01:12,029
Luis checks integration fit.

21
00:01:12,099 --> 00:01:17,197
The next gate occurs after the twelve-task
slice reading, using the original thresholds.

22
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,827
What should happen to conflicting expectations?

23
00:01:19,897 --> 00:01:23,204
A. Resolve or expose them before execution B.

24
00:01:23,274 --> 00:01:25,258
Hide them in technical notes C.

25
00:01:25,328 --> 00:01:26,885
Promise both outcomes.

26
00:01:26,955 --> 00:01:28,406
The best answer is A.

27
00:01:28,476 --> 00:01:32,401
Unresolved scope expectations
are a delivery dependency.
